<EditorialShell title="SM'S DEX | Interactive Portfolio by Shivam Mahajan" description="Explore SM'S DEX, Shivam Mahajan's interactive Astro portfolio, accessible device controls, and public roster." eyebrow="Move 002 / Astro" heading="Building SM'S DEX" intro="An interactive portfolio inspired by nine game generations. Visitors can submit a public roster entry through GitHub for review.">
  <a slot="actions" href="/">Explore devices</a><a slot="actions" href="https://github.com/smresponsibilities/smresponsibilities.github.io">View source</a>
  <section><h2>Why this interface</h2><p>The device format gives each generation a distinct way to explore the same portfolio. The readable view keeps the content accessible when the device presentation is inconvenient. This dual-view approach ensures that visually engaging experiences do not compromise foundational accessibility, keyboard navigation, or screen reader support.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Device controls</h2><p>Visitors can switch generations, open or close the device, turn its screen off, and choose a readable view. Sound starts off by default to respect visitor environments. Reduced-motion system preferences are strictly respected across all animations and transitions.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Public roster</h2><p>The Add Pokémon form opens a prefilled GitHub issue using custom templates. A continuous integration workflow then rigorously validates the submission against JSON schema constraints and creates a pull request for review before the entry officially joins the dynamic site roster.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Tradeoffs and Architecture</h2><p>Animated interactive devices take more effort to navigate than a plain document. The site therefore includes an HTML <a href="/resume/">resume</a> and direct links to project evidence for quick scanning. The frontend is built entirely using Astro and semantic HTML/CSS without relying on heavy client-side UI frameworks.</p></section>
</EditorialShell>
